{"availability":"available","full":"YOGESH256/dyanamic-flip-screen","name":"dyanamic-flip-screen","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2024-10-06T12:48:03Z","updated":"2026-09-14T10:28:59Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dyanamic-flip-screen.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://dyanamic-flip-screen.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:16.477Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:16.477Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:38:16.477Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:38:16.477Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Turn wide video into tall video. Steer the crop by hand while the video plays, like holding a phone camera. Everything runs in your browser: nothing is uploaded, no account, no watermark.","Auto-reframe tools guess where the subject is and often guess wrong. Pro editors let you keyframe the crop by hand, but that is slow. Dynamic Flip records your hand movement as the crop path, then renders it with hardware-accelerated WebCodecs."],"features":["Drop in MP4, MOV, or WebM. Play, pause, seek, speed 0.5x to 2x, volume.","Crop box locked to 9:16, 9:18, 4:5, 1:1, 3:4, or 4:3. Full player height by default. Movable and resizable, always inside the frame.","Live preview of the cropped region in a fixed-size panel, updated every animation frame.","Record clip. Press Record where the clip should start, steer the frame while it plays, press Stop where it should end. That saves your moves (time, crop rectangle, volume, playback rate, every frame) and marks the clip…","Quick fixes. Grabbing the frame while the video plays re-records just that part. Dragging while paused fixes a single moment."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/YOGESH256/dyanamic-flip-screen/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4d17755b9f1641126f76df646c810d2ba23332201cd34b57691bb3cd2a089d76","extractedAt":"2026-1